            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Cementitious, elastomeric, or epoxy — which basement coating chemistry is best?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Cementitious coatings like DRYLOK bond into the pores of bare masonry and offer the best balance of PSI rating, cost, and ease of DIY application, making them the right default choice for most basements. Elastomeric acrylic coatings like Foundation Armor stay flexible and bridge hairline cracks that rigid cementitious films will eventually crack along. Epoxy-modified coatings like Sika WaterGuard sacrifice flexibility for the best chemical and abrasion resistance, making them the right choice for basement workshops, garages, or areas exposed to oil, gasoline, or road salt.
            </p>
